 [? if year = 1919 and month = 2 and weeks = 1: The <span style="color: #000000;">**Re**</span><span style="color: #C00000;">**pub**</span><span style="color: #D3C24D;">**lic**</span> is barely three months old. Out of revolution, mutiny, and the Kaiser's abdication, we have built something never seen before in <span style="color: #000000;">**Ge**</span><span style="color: #C00000;">**rm**</span><span style="color: #D3C24D;">**an**</span> history, a <span style="color: #000000;">**Re**</span><span style="color: #C00000;">**pub**</span><span style="color: #D3C24D;">**lic**</span>. We are currently one of the three founding parties part of the <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> Coalition of the SPD, the Z, and ourselves. ?]

 [? if year = 1919 and month = 2 and weeks = 1: But the peace with the <span style="color: #002654;">Western</span> <span style="color: #D7141A;">Allies</span> has not yet been made, the country is still recovering from a war that broke its economy, and armed men who never demobilized still roam the streets under nobody's firm control. Now, the task of <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Social Liberalism</span> is to draft a constitution, make peace with the <span style="color: #002654;">Ent</span><span style="color: #D7141A;">ente</span> and rebuild the economy.  ?]

 [? if year = 1919 and month = 2 and weeks = 2: Friedrich Ebert is officialized as President by the National Assembly. <hr style="border:0;border-top:2.3px solid #000;margin:10px 0;"> The massive Seattle General Strike in the <span style="color: #B31942;">**Unit**</span><span style="color: #DDD"> **ed St**</span><span style="color: #0A3161"> **ates**</span> has ended after the summoning of Federal troops and the labour walkout's end. <hr style="border:0;border-top:2.3px solid #000;margin:10px 0;"> A skirmish has taken place in the Russo-Polish border, named the Battle Of Bereza Kartuska, this is a bad sign for the east, to say the least. ?]

 [? if year = 1919 and month = 3 and weeks = 2: Eugene V. Debs, socialist and anti-War activist, enters prison at the Atlanta Federal Penitentiary for speaking out against conscription in the <span style="color: #E60000;">**United**</span><span style="color: #F8F8FF"> **States**</span> during World War I. ?]

 [? if year = 1919 and month = 7 and weeks = 4: Kaarlo Juho Ståhlberg, an ardent Republicanist, was elected to become the first President since <span style="color: #002F6C;">**Fin**</span><span style="color: #FFFFFF;">**nish**</span> independence from the <span style="color: #FFFFFF;">**Russ**</span><span style="color: #0039A6;">**ian Em**</span><span style="color: ##D52B1E;">**pire**</span>. This comes as an upset, as General Mannerhein, instrumental for the white's Win in the <span style="color: #002F6C;">**Fin**</span><span style="color: #FFFFFF;">**nish**</span> Civil War, was expected to win the Election. ?] 

 [? if year = 1920 and month = 2 and weeks = 1: The DAP, an insignificant far-right völkisch party in Munich led by Anton Drexler and Adolf Hitler has held its biggest meeting yet, with 2000 people, where they announced their renaming to the National Socialist German Workers Party (NSDAP). ?] 

